==English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|en|encountre}} {{qualifier|obsolete}}
* {{l|en|incounter}} {{qualifier|archaic}}
* {{l|en|incountre}} {{qualifier|obsolete}}

===Etymology===
{{defdate|circa 1297}} From {{etyl|xno|en}} {{m|fro|encountrer}}, {{etyl|fro|en}} {{m|fro|encontrer||to confront}}, from {{m|fro|encontre||against, counter to}}, from {{etyl|LL.|en}} {{m|la|incontra||in front of}} itself from {{etyl|la|en}} {{m|la|in-||in}} + {{m|la|contra||against}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|en-us-encounter.ogg|Audio (US)|lang=en}}
* {{rhymes|aʊntə(r)|lang=en}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[meet]] (someone) or find (something) [[unexpectedly]].
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[confront]] (someone or something) face to face.
# {{lb|en|ambitransitive}} To [[engage]] in [[conflict]], as with an enemy.
#: ''Three armies '''encountered''' at Waterloo.''
#* Shakespeare
#*: I will '''encounter''' with Andronicus.

