===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# An [[unplanned]] or [[unexpected]] [[meeting]].
#: {{ux|en|Their '''encounter''' was a matter of chance.}}
#* {{RQ:Chmbrs YngrSt|III}}
#*: That was Selwyn's first '''encounter''' with the Ruthvens. A short time afterward at the opera Gerald dragged him into a parterre to say something amiable to one of the amiable débutante Craig girls—and Selwyn found himself again facing Alixe.
# A [[hostile]] meeting; a [[confrontation]] or [[skirmish]].
# A sudden, often violent [[clash]], as between combatants.
# {{lb|en|sports}} A [[match]] between two opposing sides.
#* {{quote-journal|date=October 29, 2011|author=Phil McNulty|work=BBC Sport
|title=[http://news.bbc.co.uk/sport2/hi/football/15413593.stm Chelsea 3-5 Arsenal]
|passage=Andre Santos equalised and the outstanding Theo Walcott put Arsenal ahead for the first time before Juan Mata's spectacular strike set up the finale for an enthralling '''encounter'''.}}

